52206.body:
As observed in HeaderConsistency check performed in https://github.com/cms-sw/cmssw/pull/52012#issuecomment-6202949751, FlatOccupancy objects mapper header file utilises C's `floor` instead of `std::floor`.
Additionally to this, this PR strips the implementation out of the header file to reduce compilation time of consumer MuonAlignmentFromReference plugin. In addition:

- replaces `std::cout` by MessageLogger printers ;
- removes a dangling `TFile` pointer ;
- uses a hash map instead of an ordered map to retrieve objects.

#### PR validation:

Unit tests pass, `scram b check-headers` confirms the fix.

